# `gh` CLI — GitHub

GitHub's CLI (`gh`) is installed via Homebrew as a standalone binary. It authenticates via `gh auth login` and operates against `github.com` by default.

See **[docs/gh-guide.md](../../docs/gh-guide.md)** for the full command reference (issues, PRs, CI, auth).

## Remote detection

`gh` reads the git remote URL from the current repo. It works with any `github.com` remote.

## Auth

```bash
# Login (interactive browser flow or token)
gh auth login

# Check status
gh auth status

# Switch between accounts
gh auth switch
```

## Draft / Ready status

GitHub tracks draft status as a PR property (not title-based):

```bash
# Create a draft PR
gh pr create --draft --title "my change" --body-file <path>

# Mark ready
gh pr ready <PR>

# Mark draft
gh pr ready <PR> --undo
```

## Checking CI status

```bash
# View latest CI run
gh run view

# List recent runs
gh run list

# Watch a run live
gh run watch <run-id>
```

## PR comments

```bash
# Comment on a PR
gh pr comment <PR> --body-file <path>
```

## Viewing PR diffs and changed files

GitHub uses a top-level `pr diff` subcommand (unlike `fj`, which nests it under `pr view`):

```bash
# View the diff
gh pr diff <PR#>

# Patch format (pipeable to git apply)
gh pr diff <PR#> --patch

# Only list changed file names (no diffs)
gh pr diff <PR#> --name-only

# Exclude files by glob (repeatable)
gh pr diff <PR#> --exclude "**/*.lock"

# Open in browser
gh pr diff <PR#> --web

# List files changed in the PR
gh pr view <PR#> --json files --jq '.files[].path'
```

Without an argument, `gh pr diff` targets the PR for the current branch.

